# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# front4 PROD env TEMPLATE — Bispharma read-plane re-point (roadmap W3.4)
#
# ⚠ THIS IS A REFERENCE TEMPLATE, NOT A LIVE CONFIG.
#   - It is NOT front4/.env.production and is NOT built or shipped from here.
#   - front4 is a separate repo (sibling `front4`), not a submodule of this stack.
#   - The W3 read-plane flags below are PRESENT-BUT-OFF (commented) so the exact
#     shape of the flip is reviewable this week WITHOUT changing what front4 reads.
#   - The live flip = uncomment the three VITE_REFDATA_* lines in the REAL
#     front4/.env.production and rebuild — and ONLY after the §5 health-gate in
#     docs/adr/reference/production-w3-readplane-repoint.md is fully green +
#     USER sign-off. See that doc, §2 and §5.
#
# Today's real front4/.env.production (legacy read plane — DO NOT change here):
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api4.packiot.com/
#   VITE_EDGE_API=https://edge.api4.packiot.com
# → reads come from legacy Hasura Cloud (gqlpiot.packiot.com) + back4.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Legacy product API + edge-api bases (UNCHANGED at go-live — writes/PO control
# still flow through edge-api; only READS move to refdata).
VITE_API_URL=https://api4.packiot.com/
VITE_EDGE_API=https://edge.api4.packiot.com

# ── W3.4 read-plane re-point → new-prod refdata (GATED — keep commented until G5) ──
# Uncommenting these three + rebuilding front4 cuts Bispharma's reads over from
# the legacy plane onto new-prod refdata → the single F3 DB.
#
#   VITE_REFDATA_API_URL   — the dedicated no-Authentik refdata vhost (roadmap §1.3);
#                            NOT behind the Authentik-wrapped *.prod services vhosts.
#   VITE_REFDATA_ENABLED   — master gate: turns on the refdata transport.
#   VITE_REFDATA_ANALYTICS — SECOND, independent gate for the Overview + analytics
#                            pages. ANDed with _ENABLED. NOTE: the analytics hook is
#                            refdata-ONLY (no Hasura fallback) — flipping this before
#                            the health-gate passes blanks dashboards. Flip LAST.
#
# VITE_REFDATA_API_URL=https://refdata.prod.packiot.app
# VITE_REFDATA_ENABLED=true
# VITE_REFDATA_ANALYTICS=true

# ── Auth: Firebase now, Cognito later (ADR-0034) ──────────────────────────────
# Bispharma stays on Firebase at go-live. front4 sends the SAME Firebase ID token
# it already sends to Hasura/back4; refdata dual-verifies it (issuer-agnostic).
# Cognito is a later, additive step (provision prod pool → seed id_user_cognito →
# flip COGNITO_AUTH_ENABLED=true in refdata + set these). Public SPA identifiers,
# no secret — kept OFF until a prod pool exists.
# VITE_AUTH_COGNITO_ENABLED=false
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=<prod-pool-id>
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID=<prod-app-client-id>
# VITE_COGNITO_LINK_ENABLED=false
